{"type": "elementor", "siteurl": "https://gototherapy.co.uk", "elements": [{"id": "8773c9d", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "flex_direction": "column", "_css_classes": "gt-section gt-section--tight gt-hero", "flex_gap": {"column": "20", "row": "20", "unit": "px", "size": 20}}, "elements": [{"id": "a715e4e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Online counselling", "header_size": "p", "_css_classes": "gt-eyebrow"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "48dd740", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "The same checks, from your own room.", "header_size": "h1", "_css_classes": "gt-h1"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "89a58f3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Online counselling is therapy by video call or phone with a qualified therapist, instead of in a room together. The therapists listed here for online work have had their registration, insurance and supervision checked by a person, exactly as for in-person work. It suits people who cannot travel, have unpredictable hours, or find it easier to talk from home.</p>", "_css_classes": "gt-answer"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "f9386bd", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "_css_classes": "gt-actions", "flex_direction_tablet": "row", "flex_direction_mobile": "row", "flex_align_items": "center", "flex_gap": {"column": "12", "row": "12", "unit": "px", "size": 12}, "flex_gap_tablet": {"column": "32", "row": "32", "unit": "px", "size": 32}, "flex_wrap": "wrap"}, "elements": [{"id": "aef3416", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "button", "settings": {"text": "Therapists who work online", "link": {"url": "/find-a-therapist/?online=1", "is_external": "", "nofollow": ""}, "_css_classes": "", "size": "md"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "0e7e3b3", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "flex_direction": "column", "_css_classes": "gt-section gt-section--tight gt-section--flush-top", "flex_gap": {"column": "20", "row": "20", "unit": "px", "size": 20}}, "elements": [{"id": "9800368", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "_css_classes": "gt-row", "flex_direction_tablet": "column", "flex_direction_mobile": "column", "flex_align_items": "center", "flex_gap": {"column": "48", "row": "32", "unit": "px", "size": 48}, "flex_gap_tablet": {"column": "32", "row": "32", "unit": "px", "size": 32}}, "elements": [{"id": "4e095bd", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "_css_classes": "gt-col", "flex_gap": {"column": "20", "row": "20", "unit": "px", "size": 20}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 50.0}, "width_tablet": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "51940ea", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "image", "settings": {"image": {"url": "https://aririkushimeikito.github.io/gototheraphy/assets/images/desk-laptop-candle-1100.jpg", "id": 0, "alt": "A desk seen from above with an open laptop, a notebook, a small plant and a lit candle", "source": "library"}, "image_size": "full", "caption_source": "none", "_css_classes": "gt-photo gt-photo--wide gt-photo--wide"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "0727553", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "_css_classes": "gt-col gt-prose", "flex_gap": {"column": "20", "row": "20", "unit": "px", "size": 20}, "width": {"unit": "%", "size": 50.0}, "width_tablet": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}, "width_mobile": {"unit": "%", "size": 100}}, "elements": [{"id": "1d68545", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Can I have therapy online?", "header_size": "h2", "_css_classes": "gt-h2"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "75622f8", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Yes. Most of the therapists listed here offer online sessions, by video or by phone, and many work that way entirely. You choose a therapist in the same way, read the same four questions, and see the same list of what was checked. The only practical difference is where you sit.</p>", "_css_classes": ""}, "elements": []}, {"id": "5646960", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Who does online counselling suit?", "header_size": "h2", "_css_classes": "gt-h2"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "2d1ba9f", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>People who live somewhere with few therapists, or where the one they want to see is an hour away. People with caring responsibilities or shift patterns that make a fixed weekly journey impossible. People who do not want to be seen walking into a building. People who find it easier to say difficult things when they are not in the same room. None of these is a lesser reason.</p>", "_css_classes": ""}, "elements": []}, {"id": "20df487", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "What changes when the room is a screen?", "header_size": "h2", "_css_classes": "gt-h2"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "5b15b0b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You have to make the room. A door that closes, headphones if you share a wall, and a slot when you will not be interrupted. Some people sit in the car. The therapist will usually check at the start that you are somewhere private.</p>", "_css_classes": ""}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e23b7ac", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>The ending is more abrupt. In person, there is a corridor and a street. Online, the call ends and you are back in your kitchen. Many people find it helps to keep ten minutes clear afterwards.</p>", "_css_classes": ""}, "elements": []}, {"id": "193fe04", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Some things are harder to read on a screen, and a good therapist will ask more often whether something has landed. You are allowed to say “I would rather do this in person” if you find that out after a few sessions.</p>", "_css_classes": ""}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "b7d0b35", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "flex_direction": "column", "_css_classes": "gt-section gt-section--tight gt-band", "flex_gap": {"column": "20", "row": "20", "unit": "px", "size": 20}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#EBE5DB"}, "elements": [{"id": "5183ef8", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Setting it up so it works", "header_size": "h2", "_css_classes": "gt-h2"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "333c477", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "html", "settings": {"html": "<ul class=\"feature-list\" style=\"margin-top:2rem;max-width:62ch\">\n<li class=\"feature-list__item\"><span class=\"feature-list__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" width=\"18\" x=\"3\" y=\"4\"></rect><path d=\"M8 21h8M12 18v3\"></path></svg></span><div><p class=\"feature-list__title\">Ask what they use</p><p class=\"feature-list__text\">Most therapists use a mainstream video service. Ask before the first session, and test it once so the first ten minutes are not spent on the software.</p></div></li>\n<li class=\"feature-list__item\"><span class=\"feature-list__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M3 18v-6a9 9 0 0 1 18 0v6\"></path><path d=\"M21 19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-3a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3zM3 19a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h1a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H3z\"></path></svg></span><div><p class=\"feature-list__title\">Headphones, if you can</p><p class=\"feature-list__text\">They keep the therapist's voice private and make it easier to hear the quiet parts.</p></div></li>\n<li class=\"feature-list__item\"><span class=\"feature-list__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 7v5l3 2\"></path></svg></span><div><p class=\"feature-list__title\">Keep the edges clear</p><p class=\"feature-list__text\">Five minutes before, ten after. The session is the same length as in person; the transitions are yours to make.</p></div></li>\n<li class=\"feature-list__item\"><span class=\"feature-list__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M9 12l2 2 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M12 3 4 6v6c0 5 3.5 8.5 8 9 4.5-.5 8-4 8-9V6z\"></path></svg></span><div><p class=\"feature-list__title\">Check the same things</p><p class=\"feature-list__text\">Online therapists are checked identically: register, insurance, supervision, identity. If a website offers therapy online with no register named, that is worth noticing.</p></div></li>\n</ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "adac1a4", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "_css_classes": "gt-actions", "flex_direction_tablet": "row", "flex_direction_mobile": "row", "flex_align_items": "center", "flex_gap": {"column": "12", "row": "12", "unit": "px", "size": 12}, "flex_gap_tablet": {"column": "32", "row": "32", "unit": "px", "size": 32}, "flex_wrap": "wrap"}, "elements": [{"id": "4ec50cd", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "button", "settings": {"text": "Search online therapists", "link": {"url": "/find-a-therapist/?online=1", "is_external": "", "nofollow": ""}, "_css_classes": "", "size": "md"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1c1bac7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "button", "settings": {"text": "Read: Can I have therapy online?", "link": {"url": "/stories/can-i-have-therapy-online/", "is_external": "", "nofollow": ""}, "_css_classes": "gt-button-ghost", "size": "md"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}]}